# Go build artifacts
/statusgen/statusgen
/tools/freshness/freshness
/tools/pairedversions/pairedversions
/tools/claimguard/claimguard
/qualgen/qualgen
*.exe
*.test
*.out
# ...but the sweep lane's committed canned-linter-output fixtures (quality/16)
# legitimately use the .out extension — they are test inputs, not build
# artifacts. Un-ignore exactly that path.
!/qualgen/testdata/sweep/canned/*.out

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
# sed -i.bak / editor / hand-made backup scratch (e.g. a `cp ... leaksweep.bak`
# of a workflow before an edit) must never pollute git status or be committed.
*.bak

# Built binaries land in tools/ via release, not committed as source
/tools/statusgen

# Desk worktrees created under the portable sanctioned prefix (deskwt add / role-init on
# Windows, where the /private/tmp prefix is not a usable absolute path — #656). The
# `.claude/` dir itself carries tracked files (guardrails), so ignore only this subtree.
/.claude/worktrees/

# The multi-root fixture root's GENERATED boards (assay-selfcontain/01). Its
# sources are committed; its output is not — a checked-in copy of a generated
# board is a stale value waiting to be mistaken for the expected one.
/statusgen/testdata/stubroot/STATUS.md
/statusgen/testdata/stubroot/docs/streams/INTAKE.md
/statusgen/testdata/stubroot/docs/streams/FINDINGS.md

# Codex project config: shareable config is committed; local state and
# secrets are not. Credentials are forwarded from the environment
# (`env_vars = [...]` in config.toml), never inlined.
/.codex/*
!/.codex/config.toml
!/.codex/hooks.json
!/.codex/rules/
!/.codex/prompts/

# The credits resolver's fixture REPOSITORY (contributor-trust/09). Built by
# tools/changelog/testdata/make-credits-fixture.sh — it has to be a real git
# history (an adding commit, a merge commit, a squash landing), which cannot be
# committed inside this repository, and which must not resolve against this
# repository's own history. See that script's header.
/tools/changelog/testdata/credits-fixture-repo/
